{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/y90nupkv","slide":1,"text":"Candidate inference-retrieval architecture. Original paired RGB/SAR and example map retained from v6. Example output is not established as the user model prediction. All new building support cards, feature planes, token links, and partitions are editable schematic diagrams, not data visualizations. Drawing references: Superpixel Transformers for Efficient Semantic Segmentation, Fig. 2, https://arxiv.org/html/2309.16889v2 (pixel/region association and unfolding; its hard drawing stands for soft assignments). RAC, CVPR 2022, Fig. 1, https://arxiv.org/pdf/2202.11233 (external memory and query/support separation). We borrow visual vocabulary only, not their model operations. Existing computational dependencies retained: F/R/P to regions, T_A to key and attention query, valid Top-K on train-only memory, labels/masks to support aggregation, Q to unpool. Shared attention per support; 3 supports illustrate arbitrary K. No support gives zero update. Dashed arrows denote offline construction. RGB/SAR provenance inherited: BRIGHT ESSD 2025 Fig.6, Turkey example, imagery credits require original-source acknowledgement."}